error[E1302]: `peek`'s parameter `p` carries a raw pointer, but this boundary stays fully safe
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:13
  |
1 | pub fn peek(p: *u8) -> int { 0 }
  |             ^ `*T` crosses the boundary here
  |
  = note: unsafety never appears in types crossing a module's boundary — there are no `unsafe
    fn`s; the proof lives at the `unsafe` block and the module is the audit granule. A `*T`
    may stand in a module-private fn's signature or at the C membrane (`export`/`extern
    "c"`); elsewhere pass a `handle` (revalidated per access) or a region value, or keep the
    `*T` in a module-private field.

